{
 "about": "The one-time upgrade of gamma-ink version 1 files to version 2 (docs/dev/handwriting.md 'Upgrading version 1'): gamma/ink.py upgrade_v1 + dumps and frontend/src/ink/ink.js upgradeV1 + serializeInk must turn the bytes in `v1` into exactly the bytes in `v2`, and leave `v2` byte-identical when run on it again. The law: version 2; for every stroke whose tool is pen (or absent), pen is not false, brush is absent and ch has p but no w, a w channel is appended to ch and each sample gains w = 500 + clamp(p, 0, 1000) (the multiplier 1 + (p/1000 - 0.5) times 1000), written absolute on the first sample and as a delta after it; every other stroke and every other key is kept; the output is canonical: keys sorted at every level, no whitespace, null-valued keys dropped, whole-number floats written as integers, non-ASCII text as UTF-8 (never \\\\u-escaped). Each case is `{note, v1, v2}` with both files as JSON text.",
 "cases": [
  {
   "note": "pressure pen with p: w appended, 500 + p, deltas after the first sample",
